From 75de781579dacb49033ceeb2c86f191c8ddbf130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:57:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/109] Write and copy only the modified objects of the
 object table

A light or object move rewrote every entry of the object table and copied the whole table to every device: about 55 ms per edit with 500,000 instanced objects. When only a few objects changed their own settings or transforms and nothing else the table depends on changed (geometry or an object's geometry, light groups, particles, motion type and motion sizes, palette offsets, object count), only those entries are written and copied; their attribute offsets, which the attribute update restores from the unchanged attribute map, the motion offsets and the scene object flags of the previous write are kept. The update statistics count partial updates. CYCLES_FULL_OBJECT_TABLE_UPDATE writes every object as before, as a reference. CYCLES_VERIFY_OBJECT_TABLE verifies every partial write at the end of the scene update: the device copies on every device against the host tables, then a full rewrite of every object against the partial result (objects including attribute offsets, flags, motion tables, scene object flags); any difference is a scene update error naming the object and member.

Rationale: A light or object move rewrote and copied the whole object table, about 55 ms per edit with 500,000 instanced objects.
Contract: The host and device object tables, motion tables and scene flags are byte-identical to a full rewrite; at most one sixteenth of the objects may be modified for the partial path, otherwise and for every other change the full rewrite runs; CYCLES_FULL_OBJECT_TABLE_UPDATE restores the full rewrite and CYCLES_VERIFY_OBJECT_TABLE verifies every partial write on every device and reports differences as errors.
Tests: tests/houdini_light_update_smoke.py
